<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x)}\Big[\|\nabla\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\|^{2}\Big]+\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x)}\Big[\|\nabla^{2}\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\|\Big]\leq G^{2}+F\,," class="ltx_math_unparsed" display="inline"><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.290em" minsize="2.290em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="2.290em" minsize="2.290em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.290em" minsize="2.290em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo maxsize="2.290em" minsize="2.290em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright" style="font-size:143%;">(38)</span></span></td></tr></tbody>
</table> 
<p class="ltx_p">where the last inequality again follows from using Assumption <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>.</p> 
</div> 
<section class="ltx_paragraph"> 
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3: Bounding weights <math alttext="\omega_{k}^{\prime}" display="inline"><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></math> and <math alttext="\omega_{k}" display="inline"><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></math>.</h4>
 
<div class="ltx_para"> 
<p class="ltx_p">By definition of the weights</p> 
</div> 
</section> 
</section></mtext></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> for any </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">. Therefore it follows that </mtext><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> for </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">. Hence, for any </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and any </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">, </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">
<table class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright" style="font-size:143%;">(39)</span></span></td></tr></tbody>
</table></mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">
<section class="ltx_paragraph"> 
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conclusion.</h4>
 
<div class="ltx_para"> 
<p class="ltx_p">Plugging (<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>)–(<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>) and the bounds on</p> 
</div> 
</section></mtext></mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> (</mtext><mtext class="ltx_missing_label"><span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">) into (</mtext><mtext class="ltx_missing_label"><span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">) yields </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">
<table class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table></mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> Finally, boundedness of the Hessian norm implies that </mtext></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">J</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> is </mtext><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-smooth with </mtext><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>kF</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">, i.e., for any </mtext><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">
<table class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table></mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> ∎ </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">
<section class="ltx_subsection">  
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">C.5</span> </span>Proof of Proposition <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>: Pass@<math alttext="1" display="inline"><mn>1</mn></math> degradation under pass@<math alttext="k" display="inline"><mi>k</mi></math> updates</h3>
 
<div class="ltx_proof"> 
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6> 
<div class="ltx_para"> 
<p class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">We prove the decrease of pass@1 and increase of pass@k<math alttext="underpass@" display="inline"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">@</mi></mrow></math>k<math alttext="policygradientascentseparately.Recallthepolicyupdaterulewithstepsize" display="inline"><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow></math></span>η<span class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">&gt; 0<math alttext=":\begin{equation}\theta^{+}=\theta+\eta\,\nabla J_{k}(\theta).\end{equation}\par\noindent\textbf{(i) Pass@1 desc