<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright" style="font-size:129%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;"> <span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">Gradient conflict across all threshold configurations (DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B).</span> Each panel shows agreement scores, weights, and weighted contributions for a different <math alttext="(\delta_{1},\delta_{2})" display="inline"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></math> configuration. All exhibit negative inner products, confirming robust misalignment across thresholds. The consistent downward shift from unweighted to weighted means shows pass@<math alttext="k" display="inline"><mi>k</mi></math> optimization systematically opposes pass@1 improvement.</span></figcaption> 
